  "overview": {
    "title": "The water that shapes the city",
    "p1": "Marchica — also called Mar Chica — is a vast saltwater lagoon separated from the open Mediterranean by a narrow coastal strip. It is the first thing many visitors notice, and the feature that gives Nador its sense of space.",
    "p2": "Walk the edges, watch for seasonal birds including flamingos, and return at sunset when the corniche lights meet the water. Boat or kayak options appear in season with local operators.",
    "p3": "It is not a swimming pool: conditions and access points vary. Use it as landscape and evening atmosphere as much as a single “sight”."
  },
